{"verdict": "reject", "reason": "Setting `password: \"\"` makes the ansible.builtin.user module run `usermod -p ''`, which writes an empty hash to /etc/shadow instead of a lock marker such as `!` or `*`. An empty field does not disable the password. It removes it, and PAM configurations with `nullok` then allow login with no password. In the baseline state, the unlocked hash is replaced with an empty one. In the adversarial state, the existing lock is removed: `'!$6$...'.lstrip('!')` differs from `''`, so the module changes the hash. Neither run leaves password authentication disabled. That would need `password: '!'` / `'*'` or `password_lock: true`."}
```

